CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1776179904
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/19
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGHURD DISMAYED OVER
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGLITHUANIA MOVE
OL,4,D
OL,5, Foreign Secretary Douglas Hurd has said
OL,6, he is dismayed by President Gorbachev's
OL,7, threat to apply economic sanctions
OL,8, against Lithuania.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe announcement that the republic was
OL,11,Fbeing given until Sunday to rescind
OL,12,Flaws passed since its declaration of
OL,13,Findependence came only two days after
OL,14,Fthe Soviet leader met Mr Hurd.
OL,16,FHe said he had been assured then that
OL,17,Fthere would be no sanctions.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FMr Hurd warned that there would be a
OL,20,Fpenalty to pay in the USSR's relations
OL,21,Fwith the West if coercion was used.
OL,23,D]FFromG14-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1776179904
OL,1,Vk4                               G6/19
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMANDELA CRITICISES
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGSANCTIONS EASING
OL,4,D
OL,5, Mrs Thatcher's easing of sanctions
OL,6, against South Africa is "absolutely
OL,7, disastrous" Nelson Mandela has said.
OL,9,FSpeaking before his visit to Britain,
OL,10,Fthe African National Congress deputy
OL,11,Fleader ruled out any meeting with the
OL,12,FPrime Minister this week.
OL,14,FMr Mandela said he was keen to improve
OL,15,Frelations with the British government,
OL,16,Fbut "it was regrettable that Mrs
OL,17,FThatcher has taken a unilateral action"
OL,18,                     F
OL,19,FHowever, he was highly critical of the
OL,20,FPrime Minister's planned meeting next
OL,21,Fmonth with President de Klerk.
OL,23,D]FFromG14-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
