OL,1,Vk4                               G9/19
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGLABOUR DEMANDS FOR
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGSTATEMENT ON "GUN"
OL,5, A Labour foreign affairs spokesman has
OL,6, called on the Government to make a full
OL,7, statement on the suspended shipment of
OL,8, metal piping parts to Iraq.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FGeorge Robertson said the controversy
OL,11,Fover whether the parts were in fact
OL,12,Fpart of the world's largest gun was
OL,13,F"making Britain a laughing stock".
OL,15,FHe said a major and urgent inquiry was
OL,16,Fneeded into the incident which he
OL,17,Fdescribed as a "shambles".
OL,18,F
OL,19,FMr Robertson said questions on the
OL,20,Fsubject would be tabled in the Commons
OL,21,Fwhen it resumes next week.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG14-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
